// Title: Suspicious PROCEXP152.sys File Created In TMP
// Sigma ID: 3da70954-0f2c-4103-adff-b7440368f50e
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: xknow (@xknow_infosec), xorxes (@xor_xes)
// Date: 2019-04-08 | Modified: 2026-06-29
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects the creation of the PROCEXP152.sys file in the application-data local temporary folder.
//   This driver is used by Sysinternals Process Explorer but also by KDU
//   (https://github.com/hfiref0x/KDU) or Ghost-In-The-Logs (https://github.com/bats3c/Ghost-In-The-
//   Logs), which uses KDU.
// False positives:
//   - Other legimate tools using this driver and filename (like Sysinternals). Note - Clever attackers may easily bypass this detection by just renaming the driver filename. Therefore just Medium-level and don't rely on it.
// References:
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20230331181619/https://blog.dylan.codes/evading-sysmon-and-windows-event-logging/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_susp_procexplorer_driver_created_in_tmp_folder.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceFileEvents
| where (FolderPath contains "\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\" and FolderPath endswith "PROCEXP152.sys") and (not((InitiatingProcessFolderPath contains "\\procexp64.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath contains "\\procexp64a.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath contains "\\procexp.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath contains "\\procmon64.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath contains "\\procmon64a.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath contains "\\procmon.exe")))
